+ demás partes. [Indicadores de bits](flags.md) contiene un conjunto de casos de una enumeración en
+ una sola palabra.

- ### Lazy chains
+ ### Cadenas perezosas

- A `Chain` computes its elements on demand, and remembers them. It can therefore describe an
- infinite sequence, such as every natural number, or every line a process will print, provided
- only a finite part of it is ever forced. These operations build and cut chains without forcing
- what they leave alone:
+ Una `Chain` calcula sus elementos bajo demanda, y los recuerda. Por tanto, puede describir una
+ secuencia infinita, como todos los números naturales, o cada línea que imprimirá un proceso,
+ siempre que solo se fuerce alguna vez una parte finita de ella. Estas operaciones construyen y
+ cortan cadenas sin forzar lo que dejan intacto:

= what they leave alone:
=
- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Operation
- column  Gives
- row  `x #:: chain`  the chain with `x` prepended, without forcing what follows
- row  `Chain.iterate(seed)(f)`  `seed`, then `f` applied repeatedly
- row  `Chain.unfold(seed)(f)`  the elements `f` generates from a seed
- row  `Chain.continually(x)`  `x`, repeated
- row  `keep(n)`  the first `n` elements, without forcing the rest
- row  `skip(n)`  all but the first `n` elements, without forcing the rest
+ column  Operación
+ column  Da
+ row  `x #:: chain`  la cadena con `x` antepuesto, sin forzar lo que sigue
+ row  `Chain.iterate(seed)(f)`  `seed`, y luego `f` aplicada repetidamente
+ row  `Chain.unfold(seed)(f)`  los elementos que genera `f` a partir de una semilla
+ row  `Chain.continually(x)`  `x`, repetido
+ row  `keep(n)`  los primeros `n` elementos, sin forzar el resto
+ row  `skip(n)`  todos menos los primeros `n` elementos, sin forzar el resto

= row  `skip(n)`  all but the first `n` elements, without forcing the rest
- ```
+ ```

= row  `skip(n)`  all but the first `n` elements, without forcing the rest
= ```
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- def evens: Chain[Int] = naturals.filter(_%2 == 0)
+ def evens: Chain[Int] = naturals.filter(_%2 == 0)

= def evens: Chain[Int] = naturals.filter(_%2 == 0)
- ```
+ ```

= def evens: Chain[Int] = naturals.filter(_%2 == 0)
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= def evens: Chain[Int] = naturals.filter(_%2 == 0)
= ```
